Skill: PR “Merge Confidence” / Merge Confidence Reporter
When a PR is opened, produce a merge confidence report and 
a clear next-step recommendation (approve / request changes / block), 
based on risk, test results, coverage, and security signal

Skill: Test Failure Analyzer
When a test fails, analyze the failure logs and 
code changes to determine the likely cause of the failure and 
suggest potential fixes or next steps for the developer to investigate.

Skill: Security Severity Evaluator
When a new security vulnerability is reported, 
evaluate the severity of the vulnerability based on factors such as exploitability, 
impact, and affected components, and provide a clear severity rating (e.g., low, medium, high) 
along with recommended actions for remediation.

Skill: Coverage Impact Analyzer
When a code change is made, analyze the impact of the change on test coverage and
provide a report on how the change affects overall coverage, including any areas of the codebase that may now be under-tested, and suggest additional tests that could be added to maintain or improve coverage.

Skill: Agent Decision Engine    
When multiple signals (e.g., merge confidence, test failures, security severity, coverage impact) are present for a PR or code change,
analyze all available data to make a holistic recommendation on whether to approve, request changes, or block the PR, and provide a clear rationale for the recommendation based on the combined analysis of all signals    

Skill: Issue Triage Assistant
When a new issue is created, analyze the issue description, labels, and related code to suggest appropriate labels (e.g., bug, enhancement, housekeeping) and assign the issue to the most relevant team member based on expertise and workload.        

Skill: Code Review Comment Generator
When a PR is opened or updated, analyze the code changes and generate relevant code review comments based on best practices, potential bugs, security issues, and style guidelines, to assist reviewers in providing thorough and consistent feedback.  

Skill: PR Risk Assessor
When a PR is opened, assess the risk level of the changes based on factors such as the size of the change, the complexity of the code, the number of files affected, and the presence of any high-risk patterns (e.g., use of eval, direct database access), and provide a risk rating (e.g., low, medium, high) along with recommendations for additional scrutiny or testing if needed.   


Skill: Smart PR Consistent Comment Formatter
When a PR is opened or updated, analyze the code changes and generate relevant code review comments based on best practices, potential bugs, security issues, and style guidelines, to assist reviewers in providing thorough and consistent feedback. The comments should be specific to the code changes and provide actionable feedback for the developer to improve the quality of the code.    


